    "text": {
      "en": "Size and head shape come first: a Scaup is bigger, with a rounder, tuftless head. The white at the bill base is the best clue: a Scaup has a broad white band all the way round the base of the bill, while a Tufted Duck has at most a small smudge. In good light a Scaup's back is finely barred grey."
